Short:        Simple, macOS-inspired Workbench dock
Author:       renewable-intel
Uploader:     renew.intel.soft@gmail.com (renewable-intel)
Type:         util/wb
Version:      1.2
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.4
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.1.4/3.5/3.9/3.2 (best on 3.2), 68030+ with fast RAM
URL:          https://github.com/renewable-intel/SimpleDock

SimpleDock is a dock at the edge of your Workbench screen, in the manner
of the macOS dock. Simple to use; there is a lot inside.

  - click to start, drag to rearrange, drag off to remove, drop icons
    from Workbench to add them
  - running programs: a dot and the number of copies; a click brings
    all of a program's windows to the front, Shift+click starts another
    copy, Del closes it; programs not on the dock show at its end
  - long press: a list of a program's windows - bring one to the
    front, minimise, show, close; Force Quit for a program that will
    not close
  - keys: minimise the active window, minimise all (by what is
    active), auto-hide on/off; all changeable; the hotkey can be the
    middle mouse button
  - drop files onto a program to open them with it, into a drawer to
    copy them, into a Shell window to type their paths - an archive
    gets the command that unpacks it
  - labels below the icons, on hover, or labels only; six colours or
    your own; solid or transparent; auto-hide with a hotkey
  - a settings window (simple side and Advanced), one plain text
    settings file, the same keywords as tooltypes
  - more than one dock: Save as... makes another, placed beside the
    first and reached from its settings
  - ARexx port SIMPLEDOCK: show/hide, icons, every setting
  - optional crash reports, to send with a bug report

Minimum: AmigaOS 3.2, or 3.1.4, 3.5 or 3.9, and a 68030 with fast RAM.
Recommended: a 68040/68060 or a PiStorm / Emu68 system, and a graphics
card (Picasso96) with a 16- or 24-bit screen mode. AGA screens work,
more slowly.

Nothing to install: put the drawer anywhere and double-click SimpleDock.
The guide (SimpleDock.guide, for MultiView) has everything, one short
page per topic; the ReadMe is the same text in one file.

